1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:01,477
Seven witnesses saw

2
00:00:01,497 --> 00:00:03,003
the killer's face.

3
00:00:03,274 --> 00:00:04,067
Not one of them

4
00:00:04,087 --> 00:00:05,395
could describe it.

5
00:00:05,944 --> 00:00:07,671
Because in this city...

6
00:00:07,697 --> 00:00:09,482
nobody has a face.

7
00:00:10,115 --> 00:00:11,047
It rains here

8
00:00:11,067 --> 00:00:12,399
most nights.

9
00:00:12,689 --> 00:00:13,621
Under an umbrella,

10
00:00:13,641 --> 00:00:14,295
every man

11
00:00:14,315 --> 00:00:15,728
looks the same.

12
00:00:15,882 --> 00:00:16,884
I'm the one they call

13
00:00:16,904 --> 00:00:17,673
when that becomes

14
00:00:17,693 --> 00:00:18,711
a problem.

15
00:00:19,157 --> 00:00:20,228
You'd think crimes

16
00:00:20,248 --> 00:00:22,144
get solved with faces,

17
00:00:22,164 --> 00:00:22,945
fingerprints,

18
00:00:22,965 --> 00:00:24,436
and witnesses.

19
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:24,988
Here,

20
00:00:25,008 --> 00:00:26,219
our hands are lines,

21
00:00:26,239 --> 00:00:27,907
our faces are circles...

22
00:00:27,934 --> 00:00:29,063
and every witness

23
00:00:29,083 --> 00:00:30,693
describes everyone.

24
00:00:31,123 --> 00:00:32,020
So when the rain

25
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:33,193
murders began,

26
00:00:33,213 --> 00:00:33,854
the department

27
00:00:33,874 --> 00:00:35,190
gave up fast.

28
00:00:35,210 --> 00:00:36,200
Four victims.

29
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:37,523
Four rainy nights.

30
00:00:37,543 --> 00:00:38,522
One burnt match

31
00:00:38,542 --> 00:00:40,198
beside every body.

32
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:41,816
But here's what

33
00:00:41,836 --> 00:00:43,864
the academy never teaches.

34
00:00:43,961 --> 00:00:44,672
People can hide

35
00:00:44,692 --> 00:00:45,566
their faces.

36
00:00:45,586 --> 00:00:46,356
Nobody can hide

37
00:00:46,376 --> 00:00:47,324
their habits.

38
00:00:48,307 --> 00:00:49,100
The killer only

39
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,203
worked in the rain.

40
00:00:50,223 --> 00:00:51,097
Always at seven

41
00:00:51,117 --> 00:00:52,211
minutes past three.

42
00:00:52,231 --> 00:00:53,035
Like he was keeping

43
00:00:53,055 --> 00:00:54,050
an appointment.

44
00:00:55,207 --> 00:00:56,522
Every match was torn

45
00:00:56,542 --> 00:00:57,091
from the left

46
00:00:57,111 --> 00:00:58,078
side of the book.

47
00:00:58,098 --> 00:00:59,639
He was left-handed.

48
00:00:59,735 --> 00:01:00,853
That narrowed it down

49
00:01:00,873 --> 00:01:02,646
to half the city.

50
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:04,059
His footprints

51
00:01:04,079 --> 00:01:05,516
told me more.

52
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:06,579
Short step,

53
00:01:06,599 --> 00:01:07,658
long step.

54
00:01:07,678 --> 00:01:09,028
He walked with a limp.

55
00:01:09,048 --> 00:01:10,004
Now it was a quarter

56
00:01:10,024 --> 00:01:11,007
of the city.

57
00:01:11,815 --> 00:01:12,421
One witness

58
00:01:12,441 --> 00:01:14,075
remembered something.

59
00:01:14,624 --> 00:01:15,336
Not a face.

60
00:01:15,356 --> 00:01:16,525
A color.

61
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,401
In a sea of umbrellas...

62
00:01:18,421 --> 00:01:19,950
one was red.

63
00:01:20,998 --> 00:01:22,754
Then I found the thread.

64
00:01:22,774 --> 00:01:24,310
All four victims sat

65
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:25,993
on the jury that freed

66
00:01:26,013 --> 00:01:27,693
the Holloway killer.

67
00:01:28,022 --> 00:01:28,663
The man who

68
00:01:28,683 --> 00:01:30,433
murdered my partner.

69
00:01:31,032 --> 00:01:32,034
Someone was finishing

70
00:01:32,054 --> 00:01:33,746
what the court wouldn't.

71
00:01:34,036 --> 00:01:35,188
I chased that red

72
00:01:35,208 --> 00:01:35,966
umbrella through

73
00:01:35,986 --> 00:01:37,759
every alley in town.

74
00:01:38,049 --> 00:01:39,050
All I ever caught

75
00:01:39,070 --> 00:01:40,715
was a warm match.

76
00:01:41,398 --> 00:01:43,438
One juror was left.

77
00:01:43,535 --> 00:01:44,049
Friday,

78
00:01:44,069 --> 00:01:46,097
the forecast said rain.

79
00:01:46,387 --> 00:01:47,388
So I parked outside

80
00:01:47,408 --> 00:01:47,911
her building,

81
00:01:47,931 --> 00:01:48,387
and watched

82
00:01:48,407 --> 00:01:49,188
the clock crawl

83
00:01:49,208 --> 00:01:50,876
toward three-oh-seven.

84
00:01:52,357 --> 00:01:53,515
I blinked.

85
00:01:53,611 --> 00:01:54,803
Just once.

86
00:01:55,294 --> 00:01:56,192
Then I was standing

87
00:01:56,212 --> 00:01:57,427
in the rain.

88
00:01:57,524 --> 00:01:58,885
Her window was dark.

89
00:01:58,905 --> 00:01:59,791
And a burnt match

90
00:01:59,811 --> 00:02:01,967
was cooling in my left hand.

91
00:02:02,623 --> 00:02:05,325
Rain. Three-oh-seven.

92
00:02:05,351 --> 00:02:07,937
A left hand. A limp.

93
00:02:07,964 --> 00:02:08,826
A red umbrella

94
00:02:08,846 --> 00:02:10,305
by my own door.

95
00:02:10,587 --> 00:02:11,903
I'd spent months drawing

96
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:13,463
the killer's portrait.

97
00:02:13,815 --> 00:02:15,286
It was a mirror.

98
00:02:16,857 --> 00:02:18,021
The blue lights came

99
00:02:18,041 --> 00:02:19,745
seven minutes later.

100
00:02:20,073 --> 00:02:21,614
My own precinct.

101
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:23,007
I didn't run.

102
00:02:23,161 --> 00:02:23,896
Where do you run,

103
00:02:23,916 --> 00:02:24,430
when the man

104
00:02:24,450 --> 00:02:25,782
you're chasing...

105
00:02:26,110 --> 00:02:27,384
is you?

106
00:02:28,165 --> 00:02:28,644
They put me

107
00:02:28,664 --> 00:02:29,840
in the lineup.

108
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:30,711
The witness couldn't

109
00:02:30,731 --> 00:02:31,558
see my face.

110
00:02:31,578 --> 00:02:33,073
She didn't need to.

111
00:02:33,227 --> 00:02:34,884
She watched me walk.

112
00:02:36,207 --> 00:02:37,603
Case closed.

113
00:02:37,623 --> 00:02:38,688
Except...

114
00:02:38,912 --> 00:02:40,436
habits can be learned.

115
00:02:40,456 --> 00:02:41,423
Copied.

116
00:02:41,443 --> 00:02:43,065
Worn like a mask.

117
00:02:43,347 --> 00:02:44,128
And outside,

118
00:02:44,148 --> 00:02:45,677
it was still raining.

119
00:02:46,723 --> 00:02:48,943
In a city without faces,

120
00:02:48,963 --> 00:02:50,012
the hardest one to see

121
00:02:50,032 --> 00:02:51,189
is your own.

122
00:02:51,808 --> 00:02:53,186
So you tell me.

123
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:54,800
Was I the killer...

124
00:02:54,954 --> 00:02:56,878
or the perfect suspect?

